Email Templates allow you to fully customize the emails Taskip sends on your behalf. This gives you control over tone, branding, and messaging across all automated communications.

When a custom template is enabled, it **replaces the default system email**. If you deactivate it, Taskip automatically falls back to the built-in template.

## Overview

Email templates are grouped into two categories:

- **Client Emails**
- **Team Notifications**
- **My Templates** (your custom-created templates)

Each template can be customized independently.

## How It Works

1. Choose an email type (e.g., Invoice Sent, Support Reply)
1. Click **Customize**
1. Edit the content (subject + body)
1. Save and activate the template
1. Taskip uses your version instead of the default email

To revert back, simply deactivate the custom template.

## Available Email Templates

### Client Emails

These emails are sent to your clients during key interactions:

- Client Invitation
- Invoice Sent
- Invoice Reminder
- Invoice Payment Success
- Meeting Booking Confirmation
- Meeting Cancellation
- Meeting Rescheduled
- Support Ticket Created
- Support Ticket Reply
- Document Signing Request
- Document Invitation
- Form Submission
- Service Order Payment
- Deal Email Sequence
- Project Client Assignment
- Inbox Auto Reply
- Deal Meeting Client Notification

## Customization Options

Each template supports:

- Subject line editing
- Email body customization
- Dynamic variables (e.g., client name, invoice amount, project title)
- Branding consistency (logo, signature, company details)

## Best Practices

- Keep subject lines short and clear
- Personalize emails using variables
- Maintain consistent brand tone across all templates
- Avoid removing important transactional details (like payment links or due dates)
- Test templates before activating them in production

## Default Behavior

If no custom template is active:

- Taskip automatically sends the **system default email**
- No setup is required

## Deactivation

You can deactivate any custom template at any time:

- Switch off customization → system default resumes immediately

## Notes

- Changes apply only to future emails
- Existing sent emails are not affected
- Some system emails may require mandatory fields for proper delivery
